        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T15:11:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Being the person who wrote the documentation, that is NOT what is meant there 😊\n\nLook at the /sys/power/disk/ file in sysfs, that is an array of items.\n\nThis is just a bunch of stuff in one file.  Not what sysfs is for at all.",
      "parentUuid": "e1fd87d4_cd29707f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "8a73c5c6ca9426dc3270f7213af8242f41e562b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eabf49e7_96cff5b7",
        "filename": "drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf-sysfs-stats.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120612
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T17:17:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg, it is simply an array of device base names. They are all values of the same type. There is no likelihood of it overflowing the 4K sysfs buffer size since in practice only a handful of devices attach to a buffer.\n\nThere will be no functional dependency on the file. It is only going to be used for stats gathering purposes(specifically GPU memory accounting) so there is no real danger from reading a truncated file(which is extremely unlikely to happen).",
      "parentUuid": "07656a72_702cf205",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "8a73c5c6ca9426dc3270f7213af8242f41e562b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1555f76_0a7921c8",
        "filename": "drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf-sysfs-stats.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T17:25:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand the need/want to do this, but this is not ok for sysfs, and I would reject this upstream if it were submitted there.\n\nIt is a list of things, that you then have to parse in userspace.\n\nWe have had files in the past that were \"no way this is ever going to overflow the buffer\" that we are now dealing with overflows due to more LEDs in the system than people ever imagined, or more CPUs than people expected would be possible.  So to prevent this, please just do not have lists like this in sysfs.",
      "parentUuid": "eabf49e7_96cff5b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "8a73c5c6ca9426dc3270f7213af8242f41e562b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "802fd7a3_9eafcd37",
        "filename": "drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf-sysfs-stats.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120612
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T17:36:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are actually not planning to send this upstream. It is more of a stop-gap measure for the GKI 2.0 kernel to not lose features based on the sysfs statistics we are deleting :( \n\nWe already have plans to start phasing out this file starting with GKI 3.0 so we don\u0027t really have to be concerned about requirements changing in future and causing the buffer to overflow.\n\nAbout the need to parse in user-space, this should be ok since the values are all of the same type right Greg?",
      "parentUuid": "f1555f76_0a7921c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "8a73c5c6ca9426dc3270f7213af8242f41e562b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
